# Sandbox and Execution

## Providers are chosen by the host

- Execution sits behind `SandboxProvider` / `SandboxManager` in `@catamorphic/sandbox`, which holds only vendor-neutral contracts and never depends on a vendor SDK.
- Implementations are separate packages (ADR 0008): `@catamorphic/cloudflare` (default cloud provider, `CLOUDFLARE.md`), `@catamorphic/daytona`, `@catamorphic/microsandbox` (local microVMs; the desktop default), and `@catamorphic/local-process` (plain subprocesses, trusted single-tenant hosts only, ADR 0047; the stock server default).
- Hosts construct one at boot and pass `createCatamorphic({ sandboxProvider, environmentProvider })`. Libraries never pick a provider from env. Environments and allocations (ADR 0064, 0099) decide where work runs.
- Routes never call vendor SDKs; they go through core services.
- `CatamorphicCore` wraps the provider with `instrumentSandboxProvider`. Do not wrap it again, and keep the wrapper's passthrough of optional methods such as `hydrateWorkspace` when extending the contract.
- Without a provider, run routes return `503` and the client shows an error rather than crashing.

## Run lifecycle

1. Every invocation creates one `workflow_runs` row that pins a deployment artifact or session artifact. There is no test mode (ADR 0040).
2. Triggering enqueues work in Postgres and returns the Run. Hosts start workers explicitly with `catamorphic.startExecutionWorker(...)`; constructing the SDK or plugin never starts one.
3. The run coordinator advances the ordered boundary and batch scopes on that one Run row.
4. A boundary is one atomic retry scope. A batch owns paged source, per-item replay and retry, optional `defineBatchStep` coalescing inside `process`, and optional sink finalization.
5. Deployment runtimes use warm, deployment-scoped supervisors that dispatch isolated Bun Workers. Environment values travel through provider execution options, never shell assignments. Sequenced runtime events update Postgres transactionally.
6. Public APIs expose capabilities, never execution categories. `stage` and internal job kinds stay private.

## What each execution sees

- **Deployment runtime:** the immutable, verified capability snapshot under `.catamorphic/` for its artifact (`executionFiles` in `@catamorphic/parser`). Never clone the whole imported repository for execution.
- **Coding-agent workspace:** the selected checkout or managed allocation with the complete project. Preserve its root files; capability scaffolding stays in `.catamorphic/`.
- **Project data:** a local host may give its provider `projectDataDirectory`; deployment runtimes then see it as `CATAMORPHIC_APP_DATA_DIR`, separate from immutable source. Build sandboxes do not get this mount, and cloud execution does not imply data sync (ADR 0142, `INTEGRATION.md`).
- Plugin references and other staging live in host storage; every agent harness accepts the host's `pluginDirectory`.

## Step instrumentation

`prepareProjectExecution` / `prepareWorkflowExecution` in `packages/parser/src/execution-transform.ts` wraps the exact step call expressions with node ids from the parsed graph. Transform only the disposable execution copy, never user source or step declarations. Do not use regex source rewriting or monkey-patch ES module exports; module bindings are immutable, so patches silently fail.

## Coding agents

Agents implement `CodingAgentProvider`; hosts pass one provider or a `CodingAgentRegistry` as `createCatamorphic({ codingAgent })`, which enables agent sessions and routes (ADR 0038, 0050). Harnesses: `@catamorphic/ai-sdk` (in the host process, any API model; model keys never enter the sandbox), `@catamorphic/claude-code`, and `@catamorphic/codex` (pinned Codex app-server protocol). Sessions record `base_commit_sha`. Project agent definitions and skills live under `.catamorphic/`; imported projects get missing framework skills through the host tier without writes. See `.agents/skills/sandbox-agent-integration/SKILL.md` for details.
